# Defect 508, 2026-10-08 (panel 199's completeness critic), and panel 199's
# R2, ratified 2026-10-09 with *unbounded recursion is an abort*: spec `:280`
# says recursion too deep aborts, and at `-O2`, where `heroes run` compiles,
# clang turned the call in tail position into a jump, so `ping` and `pong`
# called each other until `timeout` stopped them (exit 124) where `-O0`
# printed `panic: stack exhausted` (134). The `-O2` words keep a call a call
# (`-fno-optimize-sibling-calls`, `selfhost/cli/flags.hero`), and the program
# aborts at every level. `check` lets it through: mutual recursion is no
# shape `endless_recursion` reads (panel 199's R7, filed apart). Under the
# sanitiser the runtime's guard yields to ASan, which says `stack-overflow`.
# Corrected 2026-10-09, defect 520 and panel 201's R3, ratified: `check`
# refuses it now, `endless_recursion`, and the case moved from `run/` to
# `check/`; what aborts at every level since is a cycle with a way out it
# never takes, `run/fixedbugs-520-...`, the witness that replaced this one.
function ping(n: i64) -> i64
    return pong(n)  #~ endless_recursion

function pong(n: i64) -> i64
    return ping(n)

function main()
    print(ping(1))
